# SQL Security and Parameterization

- Always use parameterized queries (`?` placeholders) for user inputs.
- Never interpolate user input directly into SQL strings.
- F-strings may be used only for static SQL structure (e.g., ORDER BY column names validated by enums) and must be annotated with `# nosec B608` comment.
- Validate dynamic parts (e.g., sort columns) against a whitelist (enums) before interpolation.

## Codebase references
- See `get_players` in [backend/app/services/query_service.py](mdc:backend/app/services/query_service.py) for the allowed-column whitelist and parameterization pattern.
